# CatDex — OpenAI Vision

## Pipeline

```
Client analyzeCatPhoto() → POST /analyze-cat (Bearer Supabase JWT)
  → server auth + rate limit
  → OpenAI Vision (model from env)
  → normalize → CatAnalysis-shaped JSON
```

- Client: `src/lib/api.ts`, URL discovery `src/lib/apiUrl.ts`
- Server: `server/src/` — prompt `catdexVisionPrompt.ts`, schema `catdexAnalysisSchema.ts`, `normalize*` modules
- Product docs: `docs/VISION_ANALYSIS.md`

## Env (server)

- `OPENAI_API_KEY` (required for real identify)
- `OPENAI_MODEL` (fallback in code; keep documented)
- Supabase JWT/service role for auth
- Optional: `ALLOW_UNAUTH_ANALYZE` (dev only — never enable in prod)

## Rules

- App never embeds the OpenAI key
- Preserve `notACat` / photo problem codes for UX (`errorCatalog` / PHOTO_PROBLEM_CODES)
- When changing fields, update **server schema + normalizers + `src/types/cat.ts`** together
- Client must try remote fallbacks when local API is down (`shouldTryNextCandidate` patterns) — don’t strand users on localhost 503

## Output expectations

Analysis may include breed, coat/color, tags/personality, suggestedName, confidence, rarity string, warnings, catCount. UI must tolerate partial payloads.
